// Client checklist: what still has to be checked in the real game client (the modding system is left out).
// Human-readable version: Reverse/CHECKLIST.md, generated from this file by tools/checklist/gen_checklist.py. Read by the
// server's checker (Systems/Checklist, GM .check and the web page /admin/checks): .check <id> runs "setup" as chat commands
// of the player, one by one (waiting for a cluster change to finish), then shows "steps" and "expect" in chat.
// Results go to data/checks-results.json, never into this file. The self-test checks every setup line against the commands.
// Fields of a check:
//   id        AREA-NN, stable; never renumber, add new ids at the end of an area
//   order     the place in the recommended route (1..n, each once; .check next follows it)
//   area      Russian area name (the grouping); title: short Russian title
//   priority  1 = core / likely broken / high impact (guesses in a SPEC, fixes awaiting confirmation), 2 = normal, 3 = cosmetic
//   players   1 or 2 (2 = a second client/account is needed; setup runs as the first player "A")
//   minutes   rough time
//   setup     chat command lines run as the player, in order (only existing commands with valid arguments);
//             {me} stands for the player's character name
//   steps     what the player does; expect: what must be seen; ifBroken: what to send and which log line helps
//   source    SPEC path (relative to Reverse/analysis/work) or commit
//   needs     only when setup uses a GM command that does not exist yet: the precise description of that command
